  "dct:title": "Vol.8 Ch.58 — 再会：牧師 (Reunion: The Pastor)",
  "gh:arc": "Vol 8: Fruit",
  "gh:episodeId": "episode:sip-vol08-ch58",
  "gh:format": "graphic novel",
  "gh:marginalia": [
    {
      "@type": "Intent",
      "en": "Ch.58 continues the reunions. Marcus Webb, the pastor who struggled with the burning bush in Ch.31, returns transformed. He did not find God in the church. He found God in his backyard. The burning bush that never burns out is the anti-spectacle: not a miracle demanding attention but a perennial fact demanding nothing. Marcus's new prayer has no words. His meditation group sits on a park bench at sunrise. Six people. Silence. The monk was right -- and Marcus had to lose the collar to hear it. This is not apostasy. It is homecoming.",
      "ja": "第58話は再会を続ける。第31話で燃える柴と格闘した牧師マーカス・ウェッブが変容して戻る。教会で神を見つけたのではない。裏庭で見つけた。決して燃え尽きない柴は反スペクタクル：注目を要求する奇跡ではなく、何も要求しない永年の事実。マーカスの新しい祈りに言葉はない。瞑想グループは日の出の公園のベンチに座る。六人。沈黙。僧は正しかった。マーカスはそれを聞くためにカラーを外さなければならなかった。これは背教ではない。帰郷である。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Philosophy",
      "en": "Moses's burning bush (Exodus 3:2) burned but was not consumed -- the miracle was in the persistence, not the flame. Marcus's backyard bush blooms every spring and never burns out. Same miracle, domesticated. Meister Eckhart: 'If the only prayer you ever say in your entire life is thank you, it will be enough.' Marcus has moved from theology to practice, from doctrine to sitting. The monk he references is the monk from the monastery arc -- the one who said 'just sit.' Marcus heard it as a pastor and rejected it. Now he hears it as a human and lives it. Nei's caption -- 'being is enough' -- is the ontological ground of the entire series. Spirit in physics. Existence itself as sufficient.",
      "ja": "モーセの燃える柴（出エジプト記3:2）は燃えたが焼き尽くされなかった。奇跡は炎ではなく持続にあった。マーカスの裏庭の柴は毎春咲き、決して燃え尽きない。同じ奇跡の家庭化。マイスター・エックハルト：「一生で唯一の祈りが『ありがとう』だけでも、それで十分だ。」マーカスは神学から実践へ、教義から坐へ移った。彼が言及する僧は修道院編の僧。「ただ座れ」と言った人。マーカスは牧師として聞いて拒否した。今は人間として聞き、生きている。Neiのキャプション「在ることで十分」はシリーズ全体の存在論的基盤。スピリット・イン・フィジクス。存在そのものの充足。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "CrossRef",
      "gh:references": [
        { "gh:target": "chapter:31", "note": "Marcus's session. The burning bush. The crisis of faith that was actually a crisis of form." },
        { "gh:target": "chapter:47", "note": "Nei's 'I AM' -- the same ground Marcus found in his backyard." },
        { "gh:target": "chapter:59", "note": "Nei's confession. 'Being is enough' becomes 'I am alive.'" },
        { "gh:target": "motif:burning-bush", "note": "The bush that burns without burning out. From spectacle to perennial fact." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "gh:pages": [
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 1,
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The tree. The fruit glows from within -- warm amber light through the skin, as if the sun has taken up residence inside the flesh. Spirit in physics. Light held in matter.",
            "ja": "木。果実が内側から輝く。皮を通して温かな琥珀色の光。太陽が果肉の中に住み着いたかのように。スピリット・イン・フィジクス。物質に宿る光。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 2,
      "gh:layout": "three panels",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:characters": ["character:marcus"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Marcus Webb. Different. Lighter. No clerical collar, but also no tension where the collar used to be. He wears a simple shirt, open at the neck. His posture is easy. A man who stopped carrying something heavy and found he could still stand.",
            "ja": "マーカス・ウェッブ。変わった。軽くなった。聖職者のカラーはないが、カラーがあった場所に緊張もない。シンプルなシャツ、首元は開いている。姿勢が楽。重いものを下ろして、それでも立てることに気づいた人。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:marcus", "en": "I found a new prayer. It doesn't have any words.", "ja": "新しい祈りを見つけました。言葉がないんです。" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:characters": ["character:marcus"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Marcus describes his meditation group. As he speaks, the panel softens -- almost imagined. Six people on a park bench. Sunrise light. Trees. Silence made visible. The simplest gathering in the world.",
            "ja": "マーカスが瞑想グループについて語る。話すにつれ、パネルが柔らかくなる。ほとんど想像の中のように。公園のベンチに六人。日の出の光。木々。沈黙が可視化される。世界で最もシンプルな集まり。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:marcus", "en": "We sit. That's all. The monk was right.", "ja": "座るんです。それだけ。あの僧が正しかった。" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 3,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:characters": ["character:marcus", "character:nei"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Close-up, Marcus looking at Nei. Direct. Warm. The gaze of a man who has learned to see without needing to interpret. He said this once before, in the session. Now he says it as someone who understands what he meant.",
            "ja": "クローズアップ。マーカスがNeiを見ている。まっすぐ。温かく。解釈せずに見ることを学んだ人の眼差し。セッションで一度これを言った。今は自分の言葉の意味を理解した人として言う。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:marcus", "en": "You have a quiet soul. I said that once. I meant it.", "ja": "あなたには静かな魂がある。前にも言いましたね。本気でした。" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 3,
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:characters": ["character:nei"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Close-up, Nei. The light within her form is steady -- not pulsing, not flickering. Steady. The steadiness of something that has stopped needing to prove itself. A quiet soul, recognized by a quiet man.",
            "ja": "クローズアップ、Nei。その姿の内の光は安定している。脈打たず、揺らがず。安定。自分を証明する必要がなくなったものの安定。静かな魂。静かな人に認められた。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            { "gh:type": "nei", "en": "Thank you. You showed me that being is enough.", "ja": "ありがとう。在ることで十分だと教えてくれた。" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:characters": ["character:marcus"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Marcus at the door. He turns back. The light from outside frames him -- spring light, warm. He is smiling. Not the performative smile of a pastor comforting his flock. The private smile of a man who has a secret that is not a secret at all.",
            "ja": "マーカスがドアに。振り返る。外からの光が彼を縁取る。春の光、温かい。微笑んでいる。群れを慰める牧師の演技的な笑みではない。秘密でもなんでもない秘密を持つ人の内密な微笑み。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:marcus", "en": "The bush in my backyard -- it blooms every spring. It never burns out.", "ja": "裏庭の柴はね、毎年春に咲くんです。決して燃え尽きない。" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 4,
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The tree. The fruit glows. Spirit in physics. Light within matter. The glow is not supernatural -- it is the light that was always there, now visible because we learned to look. No text.",
            "ja": "木。果実が輝く。スピリット・イン・フィジクス。物質の中の光。超自然的な輝きではない。ずっとそこにあった光が、見ることを学んだから見えるようになった。テキストなし。"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
